  "term": "TMA",
  "definition": "TMA stands for transmetatarsal amputation, a surgical removal of the front part of the foot through the distal metatarsals. It is used to help preserve weight-bearing and walking while removing infected or gangrenous tissue, especially in diabetic foot infection or ischemic necrosis.",
